LEAK SUSPECT #1 — CRITICAL
---------------------------
Problem: Static unbounded ArrayList accumulating ReportEntry objects
Class  : com.company.reporting.ReportCacheManager
Field  : private static final List<ReportEntry> REPORT_CACHE = new ArrayList<>()
Root   : Class static field (GC Root — never garbage collected)

Object chain:
  Class com.company.reporting.ReportCacheManager
    └─ static field REPORT_CACHE
         └─ java.util.ArrayList (id=0x00000006C3F12A80, size=248,921 entries)
              └─ ReportEntry[0] (id=0x0000000701A34500)
                   ├─ reportId: "RPT-20240917-000001" (String, 48 bytes)
                   ├─ reportData: byte[4,096] (raw report content)
                   ├─ generatedAt: java.util.Date
                   └─ queryResult: java.util.ArrayList (nested, 128 rows)
              └─ ReportEntry[1] ... (x248,920 more)

Accumulation rate: ~1 entry per 12 seconds (based on scheduler interval)
Time to fill 2GB at this rate: ~34 hours (matches server uptime of 30,244s)

Root Cause: ReportCacheManager.cacheReport() adds entries to a static List on every
            scheduled report generation. There is no eviction, expiry, or size limit.
            The list grows indefinitely until OOM.

Recommended Fix:
  1. Replace ArrayList with a bounded cache (e.g. LinkedHashMap with removeEldestEntry)
  2. Or use Caffeine / Guava Cache with size and TTL limits:
       Cache<String, ReportEntry> cache = Caffeine.newBuilder()
           .maximumSize(1000)
           .expireAfterWrite(1, TimeUnit.HOURS)
           .build();
  3. Alternatively, do not cache — regenerate reports on demand or store in DB

